    "All times are end-to-end HTTP GET times from one client. p95 is the largest sample when n=4. The provider cache state is unknown.",
    "Fully cold means that all owner application caches, including API-key and resolution caches, were bypassed. It does not prove a cold Cloudflare service or physical-disk cache.",
    "The full source objects preserve the original lengths, offsets, multipart sizes and final ETags. The eight selected source ranges also match the original hashes. This is not a separate whole-object SHA-256 readback.",
    "The full-object and packed Workers use the same WASM. Account, location, read history, runtime state and request order still limit a direct cause claim.",
    "The new full-object Worker had no read-only smoke request before its first measured cold call. First-use state is a possible confound. The separate final follow-up measures both exercised Workers.",
    "The profile ends before response headers. Its frozen clock does not measure synchronous CPU. Zero decode durations do not mean zero CPU. headersMinusPreHeaderProfileMs is a residual, not a TLS, CPU or network measurement.",
    "Streamed binary byte and success headers are taken at response creation. Expected source bytes are separate from buffered actual bytes. Exact full bundle SHA-256 proves completed body parity.",
    "The 72-call test, the earlier packed 232-call test, the dedicated CPU pass and the final 16-call follow-up remain separate. No further comparison traffic is planned."
